The arnold:filter of a RenderVar must be used for the color, depth and primId outputs of the RenderProducts given by husk

The render delegate ignored the arnold:filter authored on a RenderVar for the color, depth and primId outputs of the
delegate RenderProducts (the delegateRenderProducts render setting that husk sets), and used the RenderProduct filter
or the defaults instead: box_filter for color, closest_filter for depth and primId. The other AOVs already honored it.

husk is the only host setting delegateRenderProducts, and its layout isn't wrapped in python, so this test builds it
in C++ and constructs HdArnoldRenderDelegate directly, like test_2719. It runs one Execute() of a render pass and
checks the filter type of the output of every product, for the precedence:
RenderVar arnold:filter > RenderProduct arnold:filter > default.

See #2851 (ARNOLD-19000)

author: cyril.pichard

PARAMS: {'program_env': 'render_delegate'}
